{"id": "EUVD-2026-97710", "enisaUuid": "1199730e-9265-3c17-8b16-19e1d9d80c18", "description": "ImageMagick before 6.9.13-57 and 7.x before 7.1.2-32 contains an XML injection vulnerability in the CIP encoder, which does not properly escape input-derived data when writing Cisco IP Phone XML output. Attackers can supply a crafted file that, when converted to CIP format, injects arbitrary markup into the generated XML.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:04:34", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T11:53:04", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-3429-f84m-8qhw", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/45bb7328b36c163234f5ccb7f1d494b7c4c8c775", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/30499e67801ee8a0e70817d28b861b8616d72555", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/imagemagick-before-6.9.13-57-and-7-x-before-7.1.2-32-code-injection-via-cip-encoder"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109266", "GHSA-j882-xwcv-qg6m"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.3, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ba6d82ad-487b-358d-bea3-0d358e9f68c5", "product": {"name": "ImageMagick", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}, "product_version": "7.0.0-0 <7.1.2-32"}, {"id": "f81456a6-53f8-356c-9698-5aeb047c14ef", "product": {"name": "ImageMagick", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.9.13-57"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "fefe5885-f550-340b-aa3f-f2d45417af40", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}], "isExploited": false}